Note = {4th International Conference on Diffuse Pollution, BANGKOK, THAILAND,
   JAN 16-21, 2000},
Abstract = {In this research, we installed the storm water storage tank, which has
   three functions pollutant control, flood control and water use, to the
   end pipe of a separate system. We examined the effect of real time
   control (RTC) introduction with the scenario selection in the study area
   in the catchment basin, which has measured data. As a result, a latter
   period centering-type case is satisfied with the pollutant reduction by
   the RTC and also at the water use tank, the best control settles COD
   concentration at about 0.45 mg/l. It was clarified how to use a RTC
   method as a measure of the discharge problem from an urban area during a
   storm event.},
