Month = {FEB},
Note = {International Conference on Education (ICOED), Jakarta, INDONESIA, APR
   12-14, 2016},
Abstract = {This article observes the existence of colonial language ideology laying
   within the process of English Language Teaching in Indonesia. The long
   history of Dutch colonialism in the past and the popularity of English
   in the present day in Indonesia have caused the country to be an
   interesting object for the study of English teaching in post-colonialism
   discourse. The observation was done by distributing the questionnaires
   to the students to investigate their perception toward English language
   and how they create the dichotomy of non-native English teachers and
   native English teachers. The result of the observation shows that
   English language is seen as superior language by Indonesian students and
   native English teachers are more preferred and perceived as the only
   legitimate teacher to teach English in Indonesian school. Thus, it
   proves that colonial language ideology exists within the process of
   English Language Teaching in Indonesia.},
