   Regulatory Purposes, OOSTENDE, BELGIUM, MAY 06-09, 1996},
Organization = {Initiat Harmonizat Atmospher Dispers Modelling Regulatory Purposes},
Abstract = {This paper presents a model for dispersion of NOx from motor vehicles
   and stationary sources in urban areas. Annual average NOx concentrations
   from these sources were calculated using the Gaussian plume model. The
   calculated concentrations were compared with the observed concentrations
   at 67 air monitoring stations located in Osaka Plain. The effect of
   mechanical turbulence resulting from buildings is modelled using the
   vertical dispersion parameter, sigma(z), including surface roughness and
   initial dispersion spreads given as a function of building height and
   building-to-land ratio.},
