   and Health Engineering (WEESHE), SEOUL NATL UNIV, SEOUL, SOUTH KOREA,
   OCT 18-21, 1999},
Organization = {Seoul Natl Univ; Louisiana State Univ; Korean Soc Civil Engineers; Korea
   Water Resources Assoc; Korean Soc Water \& Waste Water; Korean Soc Agr
   Engn},
Abstract = {The numerical simulations of the rainfall infiltration and the ground
   water flow in a small city area were executed under the rainfall
   condition. In a numerical simulation of infiltration, the amount of the
   groundwater recharge from the rainfall was calculated by analyzing the
   unsaturated seepage flow of the rainfall. The numerical model of
   infiltration was applied to estimate the change in the amount of the
   groundwater recharge caused by an increase of impervious ground surface.
   In the simulation of the groundwater flow, the change in the groundwater
   level caused by the change in the amount of the groundwater recharge was
   calculated. Finally, the change in the amount of the groundwater runoff
   into the river caused by the change in the groundwater level was
   calculated.},
