Organization = {Amer Soc Civil Engineers; Amer Soc Civil Engineers, Environm \& Water
   Resources Inst},
Abstract = {Over the past 20 years, the built-up area of the urban has been expanded
   significantly, and the urbanization rate rises from 29.37\% (1996) to
   56.1\% (2015), at the same time, along with the impervious area
   increased sharply and the infiltration channel was blocked in the most
   area of the urban, manly wetlands was destroyed, river channel was
   occupied and changed it use, which changes the city's original
   ecological and hydrological characteristic, result to waterlogging
   disasters, runoff pollution, loss of stormwater resources, water
   ecological environment destruction and other prominent stormwater
   problems in water environment. In order to release above problems in the
   process of urbanization, the national state and local department has
   issued a series of code and policy documents in the past 20 years and to
   explored a new model of stormwater management. This paper the
   development of stormwater management of China was described
   systematically in recently 20 years from several points, including the
   national policy, technological changing andmanagement methods, it may
   provide a reference to developing countries about stormwater management
   in rapid urbanization.},
