   27-NOV 01, 1996},
Organization = {Int Solid Waste Assoc},
Abstract = {The productive tissue of the province of Reggio Emilia is composed by a
   great number of little and medium firms, and this fact involves a
   production of special/industrial wastes of various types that is
   pulverized on the provincial land.
   It's very useful and efficient the integration of the services for
   collection and haulage of industrial (hazardous) wastes with these
   usually managed for MSW; in fact, many firms are located into the urban
   limits and produce both industrial and urban wastes and so - with
   attention to the different ways of management of them - is possible to
   have better result, in the respect of environment.
   Moreover, we've built in the structure of Environmental Hygiene
   Department of AGAC in Reggio Emilia the plant for the storage and the
   pre-treatment of industrial/hazardous wastes, in completion and near the
   plant of the incineration of MSW (and for the treatment of process waste
   water).
   The plant has high tech. laboratories for the control of liquid and
   solid wastes coming into the structure.
   The wastes stream getting on the plant is towards some installations of
   final disposal may km far away: one of the outstanding elements of the
   management - after the characterisation of every waste, in order to
   determine the right disposal - is the optimization of the haulage.
   And so, our firm is involved in a large program for environmental
   protection, not only in the urban cleansing, being able - both for costs
   and quality of management - to give services to meet the industrial and
   the urban needs.
   Reggio Emilia is a province with about 450.000 inhabitants, in 45
   municipality, and the services of AGAC concern the water, energy and
   wastes cycle.},
