   Air Pollution, Rhodes, GREECE, 2004},
Organization = {Wessex Inst Technol},
Abstract = {For several years the Department of Mechanical, Nuclear and Production
   Engineering (DIMNP) of the University of Pisa and the Regional Agency
   for Environment Protection of Tuscany (ARPAT) have collaborated in
   research on the environmental pollution of our Region. One of the more
   critical situations with respect to atmospheric pollution is that of
   Volatile Organic Compounds (VOC) in the city of Livorno, resulting from
   the presence of an important oil refinery, other industries and traffic
   pollution. Other important VOC emission sources are related to port
   activities and to numerous small companies using solvents and paints.
   This emission scenario suggested the choice of ISC3 code to treat
   diffuse sources and CALINE 4 for emissions related to traffic on main
   roads.
   After discussion of the VOC sources in the Livorno area, the paper
   focuses on the results of the study. The need for other experimental
   data for a better characterization of the area is also discussed, as
   well as the suitability of this methodology to areas with similar
   characteristics.},
