Organization = {Wessex Inst Technol},
Abstract = {One of the main important highways that connects the north-east to the
   south, and the south part of Tehran, is the Afsariyeh highway. It acts
   as a powerful tool to transport approximately 150000 heavy and light
   vehicles daily. Owing to Iran's regulations, it is not possible to
   construct a crossing on such highways. Therefore, construction of a
   u-turn in highways can be the best decision to accelerate traffic
   movement, while increasing the safety of vehicles and decreasing the
   vehicle movement's lag time. All these factors cause a heavy reduction
   of air and sound pollution. In the present research the number of daily
   vehicles before and after the u-turn. construction, the percentage
   reduction of vehicle lag time and the considerable reduction of air and
   pollution have been studied.},
