Abstract = {Recent research suggests that musical training enhances the neural
   encoding of speech. Why would musical training have this effect? The
   OPERA hypothesis proposes an answer on the basis of the idea that
   musical training demands greater precision in certain aspects of
   auditory processing than does ordinary speech perception. This paper
   presents two assumptions underlying this idea, as well as two
   clarifications, and suggests directions for future research.},
