   Beijing, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV 13-16, 2007},
Organization = {Chinese Soc Environm Sci; Beijing Inst Technol},
Abstract = {The batch techniques were adopted to study the adsorption kinetics
   characteristics of Pb, Cd, Cu in soils from Changchun city, and the
   analytical methods of soil properties were adopted to study
   physicochemical properties of urban soils. Meanwhile multiple stepwise
   regression was used to define the chief factors influencing the
   adsorption kinetics characteristics of heavy metals in soils. The
   results showed that the pH of the soils in Changchun city approached to
   neuter or alkaline, and the amount of CaCO3 and organic matter in soils
   increased, but CEC, Eh and water content in soils tended to decrease
   gradually. According to the rate, the kinetic processes of heavy metals
   adsorbed by soils included fast phase and slow phase, and the adsorption
   rates of different heavy metals in different phases were diverse
   obviously. The kinetic processes of Pb, Cd, Cu adsorbed by soils could
   be described by the two constants equation and Elovich equation. The
   adsorption rate of Pb was mainly affected by pH, CaCO3 and the quantity
   of sand grain, and the adsorption rate of Cd was mainly affected by the
   amount of CaCO3.},
