Abstract = {The work presents the results of data processing of the groundwater
   level time series on the territory of Odessa. The author introduces a
   ``gravity-resonance exotectogenesis{''} concept. The conclusion is made
   that the change of the groundwater volume (level) in Odessa on the
   inter-annual scale is mostly controlled by three natural factors,
   namely, the fluctuations in the Earth's rotation, the tectonic
   variability of the stress-strain state of rock massifs, and the regional
   amount of precipitation.},
