Abstract = {A validated questionnaire evaluating the attitude of Chinese people
   toward wireless applications in healthcare industry was administered to
   around 1,000 people from Oct. 2006 to Jan. 2007. Investigated subjects
   include people with different occupations and in different age levels.
   Investigated content covers preferred service types of wireless
   applications in healthcare, people's concerns towards the wireless
   services, etc. Investigated methods include interviewing and dispatching
   questionnaires. The objective of the survey is to assess people's
   acceptability and requirement toward wireless applications in healthcare
   industry, called Wireless e-Health or ``WEHealth{''} for short. Result
   reveals that people's attitude toward WEHealth in China is positive
   basically; An overall analysis of questionnaires reveals some
   interesting results and some problems we should be pay more attention to
   in the future industrialization process of WEHealth systems and
   services.},
